<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="LFCAS-6810_hp-click-driver-reference">
    <title>HP Click Driver Settings Reference</title>
    <refbody>
        <section>
            <title>Supported File Formats</title>
            <p>The HP Click Driver accepts the following file formats when printing from any application via the system print dialog:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><b>PDF</b> - Portable Document Format (single and multi-page)</li>
                <li><b>JPEG / JPG</b> - Photographic images</li>
                <li><b>TIFF</b> - High-resolution raster images</li>
                <li><b>HP-GL/2</b> - HP Graphics Language files</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
        <section>
            <title>Print Quality Settings</title>
            <table>
                <title>Available Print Quality Levels</title>
                <tgroup cols="3">
                    <thead>
                        <row>
                            <entry>Setting</entry>
                            <entry>Resolution</entry>
                            <entry>Best Use</entry>
                        </row>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <row>
                            <entry>Fast</entry>
                            <entry>300 dpi</entry>
                            <entry>Draft proofs, internal documents</entry>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <entry>Normal</entry>
                            <entry>600 dpi</entry>
                            <entry>General office and marketing prints</entry>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <entry>Best</entry>
                            <entry>1200 dpi</entry>
                            <entry>Final output, photo-quality prints, retail displays</entry>
                        </row>
                    </tbody>
                </tgroup>
            </table>
        </section>
        <section>
            <title>Quickset Options</title>
            <p>Quicksets let users save and recall combinations of paper type, print quality, color mode, and scaling settings. The following quickset parameters are configurable:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Paper type</b> - Select from installed media profiles (e.g., Coated Paper, Banner, Vinyl).</li>
                <li><b>Color mode</b> - Color, Grayscale, or Black only.</li>
                <li><b>Print quality</b> - Fast, Normal, or Best.</li>
                <li><b>Copies</b> - Number of copies (1 to 99).</li>
                <li><b>Scaling</b> - Fit to page, actual size, or custom percentage.</li>
                <li><b>Crop marks</b> - Enable or disable crop marks at the edges of the print.</li>
            </ul>
            <note type="important">Quickset changes made during an active print job are temporary. To save changes permanently, click <b>Save as quickset</b> before printing.</note>
        </section>
        <section>
            <title>Color Management</title>
            <p>HP Click applies ICC color profiles to ensure accurate color reproduction. The following color management options are available:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Managed by HP Click</b> - HP Click applies the printer ICC profile automatically (recommended).</li>
                <li><b>Managed by application</b> - Disable HP Click color management when the source application (e.g., Adobe Illustrator) applies its own ICC profile.</li>
                <li><b>No color management</b> - Send raw values to the printer without profile conversion.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
        <section>
            <title>System Requirements</title>
            <table>
                <title>HP Click Minimum System Requirements</title>
                <tgroup cols="2">
                    <thead>
                        <row>
                            <entry>Component</entry>
                            <entry>Requirement</entry>
                        </row>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <row>
                            <entry>Operating System (Windows)</entry>
                            <entry>Windows 10 or Windows 11 (64-bit)</entry>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <entry>Operating System (macOS)</entry>
                            <entry>macOS 12 (Monterey) or later</entry>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <entry>RAM</entry>
                            <entry>4 GB minimum, 8 GB recommended</entry>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <entry>Disk Space</entry>
                            <entry>500 MB free for installation</entry>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <entry>Network</entry>
                            <entry>100 Mbps or faster Ethernet, or Wi-Fi 802.11 a/b/g/n/ac</entry>
                        </row>
                    </tbody>
                </tgroup>
            </table>
        </section>
    </refbody>
</reference>
